Skip the experimental Rust frontend when setuptools-rust is absent.

The Rust frontend (vllm-rs, _rust_tool_parser) is opt-in at runtime via
VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 and upstream already builds it with
optional=True. Building it would require vendoring ~600 crates for a
feature the Python frontend fully covers, so make the setuptools-rust
imports optional and return no Rust extensions when it is missing.

